// REJECTS: Valid alternatives: ['->subType(@', ',', '(']
//
// The ENTIRE GraphFetchTree lexer is one token: `SUBTYPE_START: '->subType(@'`. The arrow,
// the name, the paren and the '@' are a single indivisible lexeme. Dropping the '@' does
// not produce a subType call with a missing sigil -- it produces no subType token at all,
// which is why the parser reports the '->' and offers the composite token back verbatim.
//
// A rewrite that lexes '->', an identifier, '(' and '@' as four tokens and reassembles them
// in the parser accepts `->subType(Circle)`, accepts whitespace inside the operator, and
// accepts `-> subType(@Circle)`. All three are things legend-engine cannot read, and none
// of them looks wrong.
###Pure
function fixture::neg::noAt(): meta::pure::metamodel::type::Any[*]
{
   #{
      fixture::neg::Catalog {
         shapes->subType(fixture::neg::Circle) {
            radius
         }
      }
   }#
}
